Adds Create's palette-styled item tooltips (the ones shown when holding **Shift** or **Ctrl**) to **any item** with a single startup script. No Java code and no separate lang files needed.

## Dependencies
- KubeJS - [Modrinth](https://modrinth.com/mod/kubejs) | [Curseforge](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/kubejs)
- Create - [Modrinth](https://modrinth.com/mod/create) | [Curseforge](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/create)

>>> info
This addon is available for Minecraft 1.21.1 (NeoForge) and requires Create 6.0.7 or newer.
<<<

# Getting Started
In {st-s}:
```js
CreateTooltipEvents.register(event => {
	event.add('minecraft:stick', 'STANDARD_CREATE', {
		tooltip: '',
		summary: 'A simple _wooden_ stick. Very sticky.'
	})
})
```
Launch the game and hover over a stick while holding **Shift** to see the tooltip.

>>> info
This is a startup event, so changes to the script require a game restart.
<<<

# Methods
| Method | Description |
| `[js]event.add(item, palette, text)` | Registers a tooltip for the item. The lang keys are based on the item's translation key. |
| `[js]event.addWithKey(item, palette, langKey, text)` | Same as `[js]add`, but uses a custom lang key base instead of the item's translation key. |
| `[js]event.add(item, palette)` | Registers the tooltip without any text. The text has to come from your own lang entries (see Lang Keys and Translations below). |
| `[js]event.addWithKey(item, palette, langKey)` | Same as above, but with a custom lang key base. |

# Palettes
The `palette` parameter controls the color scheme of the tooltip. Palette names are case-insensitive.
- `STANDARD_CREATE`
- `BLUE`
- `GREEN`
- `YELLOW`
- `RED`
- `PURPLE`
- `GRAY`
- `ALL_GRAY`
- `GRAY_AND_BLUE`
- `GRAY_AND_WHITE`
- `GRAY_AND_GOLD`
- `GRAY_AND_RED`

# Text Object
The `text` parameter is an object with the following fields. All fields are optional, but `summary` is required for the tooltip to show.

| Field | Shown when | Description |
| `tooltip` | - | Lets Create detect the tooltip. The value is not displayed. |
| `summary` | Holding Shift | Main description text. |
| `condition1`, `condition2`, ... | Holding Shift | Condition labels, rendered in gray. |
| `behaviour1`, `behaviour2`, ... | Holding Shift | Text shown under the condition with the same number. |
| `control1`, `control2`, ... | Holding Ctrl | Control labels, rendered in gray. |
| `action1`, `action2`, ... | Holding Ctrl | Text shown under the control with the same number. |

Conditions/behaviours and controls/actions are numbered starting from 1. Numbers must not have gaps: everything after a missing number is ignored.

## Highlight Formatting
Wrap words in underscores to switch between the palette's primary and highlight color, for example `_Burns_ for 100 ticks`. Here "Burns" is shown in the highlight color and "for 100 ticks" in the primary color.

## Full Example
```js
CreateTooltipEvents.register(event => {
	event.add('minecraft:stick', 'STANDARD_CREATE', {
		tooltip: '',
		summary: 'A simple wooden stick with _many_ uses.',
		condition1: 'When used as fuel',
		behaviour1: '_Burns_ for 100 ticks',
		condition2: 'When crafted with flint',
		behaviour2: 'Creates _arrows_',
		control1: 'Right Click',
		action1: '_Poke_ things with it'
	})
})
```

# Lang Keys and Translations
The tooltip text is stored in lang keys based on the item's translation key. For `minecraft:stick` (translation key `item.minecraft.stick`) these are:
- `item.minecraft.stick.tooltip`
- `item.minecraft.stick.tooltip.summary`
- `item.minecraft.stick.tooltip.condition1`, `item.minecraft.stick.tooltip.behaviour1`, ...
- `item.minecraft.stick.tooltip.control1`, `item.minecraft.stick.tooltip.action1`, ...

With `[js]addWithKey`, the lang key base you pass is used instead of the item's translation key. For example, `[js]event.addWithKey('minecraft:paper', 'BLUE', 'item.mypack.paper', text)` stores the summary in `item.mypack.paper.tooltip.summary`.

Text from the text object is added as English (`en_us`) lang entries. Other languages fall back to English, so the tooltip shows up everywhere, but always in English. To translate a tooltip, register it without text and add the lang entries yourself with [[/events/ClientEvents/lang]]:

In {st-s}:
```js
CreateTooltipEvents.register(event => {
	event.add('minecraft:stick', 'GRAY_AND_BLUE')
})
```

In {cl-s}:
```js
ClientEvents.lang('en_us', event => {
	event.add('item.minecraft.stick.tooltip', '')
	event.add('item.minecraft.stick.tooltip.summary', 'A simple _wooden_ stick.')
})

ClientEvents.lang('de_de', event => {
	event.add('item.minecraft.stick.tooltip', '')
	event.add('item.minecraft.stick.tooltip.summary', 'Ein einfacher _hölzerner_ Stock.')
})
```

# Notes
>>> warning
If an item already has a Create tooltip (for example Create's own items), the registration is skipped and a warning is written to the log.
<<<

>>> danger
An unknown item ID or palette name causes an error in the startup log. If a tooltip doesn't show up, check the startup log first.
<<<

>>> info
Tooltips only exist on the client. On a dedicated server the event does nothing, so the same startup script is safe to keep on servers.
<<<
